diff --git a/docs/standalone.md b/docs/standalone.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..9cedb16
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/standalone.md
@@ -0,0 +1,99 @@
+# Standalone Windows sessions
+
+This downstream adapter adds a non-Steam entry point around the existing `play`
+graphics path. It does not patch a game's executables or replace its launcher.
+The Steam path stays the default. Wine, FEX and the graphics DLLs remain the
+unmodified signed 0.3.0 runtime used for the CPU probes.
+
+## Interface
+
+```sh
+WINEPREFIX="$HOME/Library/Application Support/Hadron Standalone/prefixes/example" \
+HADRON_SUPPORT="$HOME/Library/Application Support/Hadron Standalone" \
+HADRON_LOGS="$HOME/Library/Logs/Hadron Standalone" \
+  /path/to/runtime/scripts/standalone-run example /absolute/path/Launcher.exe arg1
+```
+
+The runtime must carry a BUILD-ID and the adapter's scripts. In this workspace,
+`python3 tools/probe/stage_t2.py` stages that tree from the verified runtime and
+the source-controlled scripts without writing through the signed loader links.
+Python and the cross compiler are development tools, not launch dependencies.
+
+The ID accepts ASCII letters, digits, `_` and `-`. The EXE, prefix, support and
+log paths must be absolute. The prefix must not be a symlink. `HADRON_WORKDIR`
+optionally selects the Windows process's working directory; otherwise its EXE
+directory is used. Arguments remain separate argv entries, never shell code.
+
+`standalone-run` cleans its environment before selecting a runtime. It retains
+explicit launch, renderer and translator settings, plus the real HOME/USER and
+system paths. It removes Steam IDs, overlay injection and unrelated host
+variables. `play` then runs the EXE directly instead of `hadron-steam.exe`, and
+does not stage lsteamclient or send Steam variables to Wine.
+
+## Isolation, locking and lifetime
+
+Each canonical prefix path gets a scope at
+`<support>/prefix-sessions/<md5-of-prefix>/`. The `owner-prefix` file confirms the
+exact path as well as the hash. Each scope has its **own APFS runtime copies**,
+under `runtimes/<BUILD-ID>`, and a `runtime` link. This costs directory entries
+and metadata; APFS clones share unchanged data blocks.
+
+Private runtime paths allow the watchdog to classify a process using mapped
+files. There is no need to read other processes' environment blocks. Prefix
+mode does not broaden the scope to all builds or other prefixes. Stop validates
+the owner-prefix and runtime location, calls that prefix's wineserver, and only
+then handles orphans whose PID start time and mapped private runtime still match.
+
+A sibling lock `.<prefix-name>.hadron-session.lock` prevents duplicate sessions
+even when callers supply different support directories. It stays outside the
+prefix so initialization can rename the staging folder. The supervisor keeps
+the lock; Wine children and the watchdog do not inherit its descriptor.
+
+Exactly one watchdog observes the supervisor throughout initialization and the
+whole session. The supervisor waits for both its initial EXE and wineserver's
+whole session, including a launcher that starts a child and exits. TERM/INT/HUP
+stop only this prefix. An app should retain the Process handle it created and
+send TERM to it; the `supervisor-pid` file is a diagnostic last-PID record, not
+proof that that PID is still the same process.
+
+Exit 75 means a session is already running or an unmanaged Wine session exists.
+Exit 2 indicates invalid paths/arguments/scope or an unsupported deep runtime
+path; exit 1 indicates preparation failure. A requested stop returns 143.
+Otherwise the initial EXE's exit status is returned after its children finish.
+
+## Prefix creation and migration
+
+Only an absent prefix is initialized. Wine creates a disposable sibling
+`.hadron-new.<pid>` folder. The adapter waits for Wine, installs the existing
+mtld3d prefix libraries, checks ARM64 ntdll, writes the ready marker, and renames
+the folder into place. Failed initialization removes only its own staging folder.
+An existing incomplete or foreign prefix is refused without deleting its data.
+
+A changed runtime ID first produces a sibling APFS prefix snapshot. Migration
+uses wineboot --update after removing the prefix's FEX disk code cache (FEX keys
+that cache on host features and settings, not on its code generator; the snapshot
+keeps the old cache). An incomplete migration retains a marker containing its
+snapshot path and fails closed on the next launch. Rollback restores both the
+snapshot and matching old runtime. Runtime-only rollback is not assumed safe.
+Old runtime copies and snapshots are retained in T2; automatic pruning is not
+part of this adapter yet.
+
+## Verified scope and limits
+
+On macOS27.0.1/M2, the actual Windows fixture tests cover Unicode and spaces in
+cwd, quoted/literal arguments, filtered environment, launcher-child lifetime,
+duplicate refusal, two concurrent prefixes, TERM and memory-limit isolation,
+runtime migration/snapshot rollback, and failed initialization/retry. The
+modified upstream runtime-version tests also pass.
+
+Wine 0.3.0's bootstrap failed when builtin paths grew past its path buffer. A
+shorter support path ran the same executable successfully. The adapter currently
+requires its selected runtime root to be at most 180 shell characters, a
+conservative preflight rather than an upstream long-path fix. Deep workspaces
+should use a short private support directory. Long user Library paths must be
+checked by the future app as well.
+
+These tests do not establish game graphics, .NET9 launcher compatibility,
+authentication, game updates, clean-Mac execution without an installed Rosetta,
+or recovery from SIGKILL/OS restart. No Steam game launch was tested; only the
+existing runtime-management regression suite and standalone path were exercised.
diff --git a/patches/fex/0006-JIT-Service-cooperative-suspension-on-conditional-back.patch b/patches/fex/0006-JIT-Service-cooperative-suspension-on-conditional-back.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..8b86384
--- /dev/null
+++ b/patches/fex/0006-JIT-Service-cooperative-suspension-on-conditional-back.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,41 @@
+From 4aad77fbb57507c769775e707a564684d41f66dc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: Alchemac downstream <noreply@alchemac.invalid>
+Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 22:03:35 +0900
+Subject: [PATCH] JIT: service cooperative suspension on conditional backedges
+
+Mirror the existing unconditional backedge interrupt check before
+emitting a conditional branch to an already-bound target. The check
+preserves NZCV, so both flag-based and register-based branches retain
+their original condition.
+
+A standalone dynamically generated x64 conditional loop hung in
+GetThreadContext with the original build; this change passes twenty
+suspend/context/resume cycles with the default MaxInst setting.
+
+Downstream only: AI-assisted work must not be submitted to FEX upstream.
+Assisted-by: LLM
+---
+ FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/JIT/BranchOps.cpp | 7 +++++++
+ 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)
+
+diff --git a/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/JIT/BranchOps.cpp b/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/JIT/BranchOps.cpp
+index c2b1d8e..219051e 100644
+--- a/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/JIT/BranchOps.cpp
++++ b/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/JIT/BranchOps.cpp
+@@ -250,6 +250,13 @@ DEF_OP(CondJump) {
+ 
+   auto TrueTargetLabel = JumpTarget(Op->TrueBlock);
+ 
++  // Like a pending unconditional backedge, a conditional backedge can stay
++  // inside this compiled block forever. Service cooperative suspension before
++  // taking it. This check uses ldr/cbz and preserves the branch's NZCV flags.
++  if (TrueTargetLabel->Backward.Location) {
++    EmitSuspendInterruptCheck();
++  }
++
+   if (Op->FromNZCV) {
+     b_OrRestart(MapCC(Op->Cond), TrueTargetLabel);
+   } else {
+-- 
+2.54.0 (Apple Git-157)
+
